<section class="od-set" id="states" aria-labelledby="od-states"><p class="od-kicker">Dataset 1</p><h2 class="od-title" id="od-states">The States Register</h2><p class="od-desc">Every state the Institute has recorded, from 5400 BCE to today: kingdoms, empires, principalities, republics and chiefdoms, with their years, type, region, capital, present-day countries and map position, and the dated relations between them: who succeeded, conquered, ruled or merged with whom.</p><ul class="od-facts"><li><b>5,468</b> states</li><li><b>11,296</b> relations</li><li><b>4,539</b> placed at a capital or seat</li><li><b>27</b> regions</li></ul><div class="od-dl"><a class="od-dl-btn" href="/epoch-institute-states.csv" download>States, CSV <span>1.1 MB</span></a><a class="od-dl-btn" href="/epoch-institute-state-relations.csv" download>Relations, CSV <span>634 KB</span></a><a class="od-dl-btn" href="/epoch-institute-states.json" download>Both, JSON <span>3.6 MB</span></a></div><div class="od-table-wrap"><table class="dataset-table"><caption>Six rows of the register</caption><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Years</th><th>Capital</th><th>Today</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a></td><td>kingdom</td><td>987–1792</td><td>Paris</td><td>France</td><td>48.9, 2.4</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/empire/joseon">Joseon</a></td><td>kingdom</td><td>1392–1897</td><td>Hanseong (Seoul)</td><td>South Korea, North Korea</td><td>37.6, 127.0</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya Kingdom</a></td><td>kingdom</td><td>1351–1767</td><td>Ayutthaya</td><td>Thailand</td><td>14.3, 100.6</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/state/kingdom-of-zimbabwe">Kingdom of Zimbabwe</a></td><td>kingdom</td><td>1220–1450</td><td>Great Zimbabwe</td><td>Zimbabwe, Mozambique</td><td>-20.3, 30.9</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a></td><td>republic</td><td>697–1797</td><td>Venice</td><td>Italy, Croatia</td><td>45.4, 12.3</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/state/kingdom-of-hawaii">Kingdom of Hawaii</a></td><td>kingdom</td><td>1795–1893</td><td>Honolulu</td><td>United States</td><td>21.3, -157.9</td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="od-cols"><summary>The columns</summary><dl><dt>States file</dt><dd>id (as in /state/&lt;id&gt;), name, type, region, broad_region, start_year and end_year (negative = BCE; an empty end year: the state exists today), approximate_dates, capital, present_day_countries (separated by &#8220;; &#8221;; empty for most of the 94 great empires, which spanned many), latitude and longitude, location_source (capital, recorded location, capital matched by name, set by hand, or approximate: the centre of the present-day country), profile_url, page_url.</dd><dt>Relations file</dt><dd>source_id, relation, target_id, from_year, until_year. Relations: colony-of, conquered-by, merged-into, part-of, personal-union-with, protectorate-of, province-of, split-from, successor-of, tributary-to, vassal-of. A succession is stored once, as successor-of.</dd></dl></details><p class="od-explore">Explore it on the site: <a href="/atlas">the Atlas</a> · <a href="/state/">States</a> · <a href="/connections">Connections</a> · <a href="/countries/">Country histories</a></p></section>
<section class="od-set" id="curves" aria-labelledby="od-curves"><p class="od-kicker">Dataset 2</p><h2 class="od-title" id="od-curves">Power Curves</h2><p class="od-desc">The curves behind the <a href="/explorer">Empire Explorer</a> and the profiles&#8217; &#8220;Rise &amp; fall&#8221; charts: a score from 0 to 10 at each turning point of a state&#8217;s history. They are the Institute&#8217;s interpretive judgements, based on the works cited in each profile, and every curve is scaled to its own peak: compare the shapes, not the sizes.</p><ul class="od-facts"><li><b>394</b> profiles</li><li><b>6,585</b> points</li><li><b>3500 BCE</b> to today</li></ul><div class="od-dl"><a class="od-dl-btn" href="/epoch-institute-power-curves.csv" download>Curves, CSV <span>607 KB</span></a><a class="od-dl-btn" href="/epoch-institute-power-curves.json" download>Curves, JSON <span>130 KB</span></a></div><div class="od-table-wrap"><table class="dataset-table"><caption>Four of the curves</caption><thead><tr><th>Profile</th><th>Years</th><th>Peak</th><th>Points</th><th>Curve</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></td><td>27 BCE – 476 CE</td><td>117 CE</td><td>16</td><td><svg class="od-spark" viewBox="0 0 120 30" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="1,17.8 9.4,15 10.6,12.2 23.5,12.2 34.8,1 46,6.6 49.6,6.6 62.5,15 74,12.2 80.5,9.4 84.7,6.6 96,15 100,12.2 103.5,20.6 114.1,23.4 119,29"/></svg></td></tr><tr><td><a href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a></td><td>1206–1368</td><td>1241 CE</td><td>14</td><td><svg class="od-spark" viewBox="0 0 120 30" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="1,20.6 7.6,15 10.5,12.2 16.3,9.4 22.9,3.8 26.5,1 38.9,3.8 40.3,12.2 54.2,6.6 54.9,9.4 65.1,15 69.5,17.8 106.6,23.4 119,29"/></svg></td></tr><tr><td><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></td><td>1299–1922</td><td>1520 CE</td><td>19</td><td><svg class="od-spark" viewBox="0 0 120 30" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="1,23.4 6.1,17.8 18,12.2 20.5,26.2 22.6,17.8 30.2,6.6 41.3,3.8 42.9,1 51.6,3.8 58,6.6 73.7,9.4 76.8,12.2 77,12.2 95.9,15 110.7,20.6 117.3,23.4 117.5,23.4 118.6,26.2 119,29"/></svg></td></tr><tr><td><a href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a></td><td>1235–1600</td><td>1337 CE</td><td>14</td><td><svg class="od-spark" viewBox="0 0 120 30" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="1,23.4 7.5,20.6 17.2,17.8 22,15 25.9,9.4 34,1 38.2,9.4 51.1,17.8 54.3,17.8 65,23.4 70.5,20.6 76.3,26.2 86.7,23.4 119,29"/></svg></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="od-cols"><summary>The columns</summary><dl><dt>CSV</dt><dd>One row per point: name, region, profile_url, year (negative = BCE), score (0&#8211;10).</dd><dt>JSON</dt><dd>One object per profile: name, region, profile_url, start_year, end_year, peak_year and points as [year, score] pairs.</dd></dl></details></section>
